 "text": "Hey there, how are you? You can use a cable organizer box under your desk and run the cables into it. It looks much cleaner than tangles under the desk. Nothing. Just checking if you needed help. Not really. You screw it into the wall under the desk and push the cables in. A few minutes with a drill. Then start there and work your way along. Each new cable needs a new hole. You can use a simple Y splitter if you only have one gap. Or a splitter off each outlet if you have several gaps.",
